<title>UK: ULSTER TV STOCK SURGES ON BID TALK.</title>
<headline>ULSTER TV STOCK SURGES ON BID TALK.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Ulster Television Plc rose 38-1/2p to 205p on Thursday on bid speculation with Scottish Media Group Plc the likely bidder, dealers said.  </p>
<p>Nearly seven million shares changed hands by 0830 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;They're talking about a bid from Scottish TV (Media),&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>No one at Scottish Media was immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>Scottish Media shares were unchanged at 642-1/2p. The company is due to complete its merger with Grampian Television on Monday.</p>
<p>Market talk also suggested that the price rise might presage a 15 percent stock buy-back.</p>
<p>-- Louise Ireland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8712</p>
</text>
